Z||000006||Rodney||04-16-2001||07:17 PM||||I'm very curious on the water injection. I have the stage II turbo. Wondering if it is worth looking into adding? Can you tell us more on how it installs and how it works. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mr.Frosty||04-17-2001||12:06 PM||||It is setup so that as soon as positive pressure is detected in the manifold(there is a switch on the right side of the intake manifold)it turns on the pump which injects straight into the intake.The man who created this setup is a mechanical genius.He installed the whole setup for $1000.00.It is worth adding as it keeps detonation away.I recommend going here for a water inj. kit <A HREF="http://www.racetep.com/turbo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.racetep.com/turbo.html</A>  they have a lot of turbo tech.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-ForSale <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||14
Z||000008||Phil||04-17-2001||12:24 PM||||Aquamist sells a very sophisticated water/alc injection system for $500||||reg||1
Z||000009||Taijiguy||04-17-2001||02:22 PM||||Water injection was most popular in the early 80's. It allows you to advance timing like crazy and counter pinging. Also it provides some minor power increases, as there is actually steam expanding within the combustion chamber. The one risk is, if you have an older engine, and the only thing keeping the motor from burning oil is crap on the rings, it will most definitely be cleaned off by the water injection system. Edelbrock, Holley, and a few other performance companies made some relly nice ones, and there were a few cars manufactured with it. I'm surprised they didn't become more popular.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||04-17-2001||02:25 PM||||I like the wheels on the fiero......and the turbo!!!!<P>give us some info of the car beside it!!!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mr.Frosty||04-17-2001||03:32 PM||||That is a 1940 Ford coupe with a 283 small block out of a Corvette.It's got a leather interior,classic VDO instruments,refinished dash,and is very clean.It was my Dad's 'rod for the last 25 years.He passed away in December,so we have decided to sell it to one of his friends.It is in need of a new paint job though.It was going to get slammed,with fattie fenders,a mustang II front suspension,shaved trim,coil overs,and a built 350 that's in parts on the bench.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-ForSale <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||6
Z||000012||KnightRyder31||04-17-2001||03:59 PM||||Hav any performence stats on that turbo fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mr.Frosty||04-17-2001||04:14 PM||||I haven't had it dynoed yet,but I would say around 200 is about right,and that's at the crank.That's when the engine was alive.I'm going to have it rebuilt soon,then tuned properly.All that I know is it spanks almost anything it comes up against,including one very upset sport bike owner.When it's driveable again I'm gonna get some numbers together.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-ForSale <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||10
